;; `(Cond -> Then ; Else)` lowers to try_me_else L_ite_else_N / Cond / cut_ite,
;; and the commit must remove the ELSE alternative TOGETHER WITH every choice
;; point Cond left standing -- that is what makes -> commit. Popping exactly one
;; (the old behaviour) removed whichever choice point Cond happened to leave on
;; top instead, so a Cond that succeeded and a Then that then failed fell
;; through into the Else branch. `pick(layered, ...)` took the catalog branch
;; for a package the frozen base already pins, and every layered query drifted
;; onto the classic answer. The one-pop fallback is kept for a cut_ite whose
;; try_me_else was not tagged (an unlabelled/unresolved instruction).
